21
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:22,280
Lesson number 11, understanding order flow price rejection.

22
00:01:23,020 --> 00:01:26,900
Knowing when the market participants are rejecting price will improve your trading.

23
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:32,680
What you want to know is, you want to know when other traders are rejecting price.

24
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:36,045
If you're in a position, you're thinking it's going to

25
00:01:36,045 --> 00:01:38,064
go higher, but price is being

26
00:01:38,064 --> 00:01:42,439
rejected, more often than not, the market's not going to go any higher.

27
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:46,540
So you should understand areas where price is being rejected.

28
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:49,300
Think in non-market terms.

29
00:01:50,020 --> 00:01:54,720
You know, sometimes it's easier for people to understand the market when they think of,

30
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:58,380
you know, everyday examples. So, when you go to the grocery store to buy food,

31
00:01:58,580 --> 00:02:01,340
and, you know, on your grocery list is you want to buy some beef.

32
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:05,720
If the price of beef has risen too much, do you buy the same amount?

33
00:02:05,860 --> 00:02:06,620
No. What do you do?

34
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:09,180
You either stop buying it or you buy less.

35
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:14,520
You know, you think of it as you're buying volume and beef slows down until you basically stop buying beef.

36
00:02:15,340 --> 00:02:18,480
You know, usually when the price is too high, you will stop buying the beef.

37
00:02:18,580 --> 00:02:19,560
You'll reject the price.

38
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:22,980
Another way to think of it is in terms of dating.

39
00:02:22,980 --> 00:02:24,403
I mean, you ask a pretty girl

40
00:02:24,403 --> 00:02:25,826
several times for a phone number, and

41
00:02:25,826 --> 00:02:27,859
she keeps turning you down, and eventually you give up.

42
00:02:28,420 --> 00:02:29,460
The market is the same.

43
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:32,774
Although there may be a heavy passive buyer or a

44
00:02:32,774 --> 00:02:35,688
passive seller, you know, at the edge of a bar

45
00:02:35,688 --> 00:02:38,602
or at the high of a move or the low

46
00:02:38,602 --> 00:02:45,597
of a move, the opposing aggressive seller or aggressive buyer will eventually give up in rejection if they can't move the price any higher.

47
00:02:46,920 --> 00:02:48,116
You know, going back to,

48
00:02:48,116 --> 00:02:49,312
you know, earlier how I

49
00:02:49,312 --> 00:02:50,508
explained, you know, in terms

50
00:02:50,508 --> 00:02:51,704
of dating, you know, think

51
00:02:51,704 --> 00:02:54,816
about, you know, if you've ever asked a girl to get married, right?

52
00:02:55,020 --> 00:02:58,860
You know, sometimes you're very desperate to get married.

53
00:02:58,940 --> 00:03:01,640
You know, just like trading, you're desperate for the market to go in your direction.

54
00:03:01,740 --> 00:03:03,468
But if, you know, the girl doesn't

55
00:03:03,468 --> 00:03:05,196
want to marry you, no matter what

56
00:03:05,196 --> 00:03:09,639
you can do, you know, if she doesn't want to marry you, she doesn't want to marry you.

57
00:03:10,100 --> 00:03:11,280
The market is the same way.

58
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:12,662
You know, you want the

59
00:03:12,662 --> 00:03:14,317
market to go up, but, you know,

60
00:03:14,317 --> 00:03:18,099
if price is being rejected at, you know, a level just past where you got long,

61
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:20,660
you know, you can hope and wish

62
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:24,380
all you want, but that's not going to make the market go any higher.

63
00:03:26,550 --> 00:03:31,350
So price rejection is important because it answers the trading question, will this level hold or fail?

64
00:03:32,050 --> 00:03:35,250
What happens is price gets to a level and cannot follow through.

65
00:03:35,410 --> 00:03:38,550
There was no more interest at that level or price levels just behind it.

66
00:03:38,550 --> 00:03:40,863
And, you know, usually a sure sign

67
00:03:40,863 --> 00:03:42,515
is the market doesn't want

68
00:03:42,515 --> 00:03:45,489
to be at or around that price level anymore.

69
00:03:45,810 --> 00:03:50,850
So, you know, you come up to a high in the market and what's going to happen?

70
00:03:51,290 --> 00:03:52,463
You know, either the market

71
00:03:52,463 --> 00:03:53,636
is going to keep going

72
00:03:53,636 --> 00:03:54,809
higher, the market is going

73
00:03:54,809 --> 00:03:57,389
to go sideways, or the market is going to sell off.

74
00:03:57,650 --> 00:04:00,970
If price is going to be accepted, price will keep going higher.

75
00:04:01,550 --> 00:04:06,030
If the market is sort of indecisive, the market may go sideways.

76
00:04:06,030 --> 00:04:09,110
If price is going to be rejected, the market will go lower.

77
00:04:10,050 --> 00:04:15,510
So order flow allows you to see areas where low volume is occurring, which is a sign of price rejection.

78
00:04:16,890 --> 00:04:18,649
You know, that's a simple explanation.

79
00:04:19,010 --> 00:04:20,703
So, you know, imagine as

80
00:04:20,703 --> 00:04:23,073
the market is going higher and higher,

81
00:04:23,073 --> 00:04:25,782
but the volume at the highs is getting

82
00:04:25,782 --> 00:04:29,507
smaller and smaller, you know, buyers are rejecting those higher prices.

83
00:04:30,090 --> 00:04:33,790
So the problem with that expression is this low volume doesn't necessarily mean that price was rejected.

84
00:04:33,790 --> 00:04:37,230
The price could have moved through a level very fast not to return there.

85
00:04:37,350 --> 00:04:40,710
So, I mean, there's going to be times where the market just spikes up and spikes back down.

86
00:04:41,230 --> 00:04:42,595
You know, usually that's

87
00:04:42,595 --> 00:04:44,302
due to, you know, some

88
00:04:44,302 --> 00:04:46,009
external factor. Maybe a stop

89
00:04:46,009 --> 00:04:47,716
got triggered. It's not necessarily

90
00:04:47,716 --> 00:04:50,447
due to, you know, overall supply and demand.

91
00:04:50,450 --> 00:04:54,890
So let's look at a chart here.

92
00:04:55,110 --> 00:04:56,150
This is a bond chart.

93
00:04:56,490 --> 00:05:02,090
You know, the market is going up and it hits the high here at 746. It starts to sell off.

94
00:05:02,510 --> 00:05:04,874
But every time we sort of try to make a

95
00:05:04,874 --> 00:05:06,529
run back up at the high, you

96
00:05:06,529 --> 00:05:09,129
know, I said we had been in an uptrend. We stop.

97
00:05:09,390 --> 00:05:10,270
Okay, what's going to happen?

98
00:05:10,350 --> 00:05:13,710
The market's either going to keep going higher, go sideways, or go lower.

99
00:05:13,710 --> 00:05:16,710
So in this case, it starts going sideways to lower

100
00:05:16,710 --> 00:05:18,810
and, you know, each bar tries to

101
00:05:18,810 --> 00:05:21,810
go a little bit higher, but you get less volume.

102
00:05:21,890 --> 00:05:24,050
You're getting single prints at the tops of these bars.

103
00:05:24,050 --> 00:05:35,150
It's rejecting the prices up here above, you know, 160.17, you know, 160.16. It's rejecting these prices and the market sells off.

104
00:05:36,970 --> 00:05:40,298
So the power of order flow is that it can show you

105
00:05:40,298 --> 00:05:45,290
more than just a price level where price was rejected. It shows you how price is being rejected.

106
00:05:46,570 --> 00:05:49,303
So, you know, one of the best signs of price

107
00:05:49,303 --> 00:05:51,216
rejection is when you circle back to

108
00:05:51,216 --> 00:05:53,949
a price again, but on lesser volume the second time.

109
00:05:54,910 --> 00:05:57,226
What do I mean by that is, you

110
00:05:57,226 --> 00:05:59,252
know, say you have a level that

111
00:05:59,252 --> 00:06:01,568
the market is, looks like it's probably rejecting.

112
00:06:01,770 --> 00:06:04,204
If we come back to that level and,

113
00:06:04,204 --> 00:06:06,334
you know, it's not showing any signs

114
00:06:06,334 --> 00:06:08,464
of acceptance, you know, and showing rejection,

115
00:06:08,464 --> 00:06:13,028
you know, then chances are the price is going to go in the opposite direction.

116
00:06:13,230 --> 00:06:14,410
So, you know, here's an example.

117
00:06:14,870 --> 00:06:17,390
This is the ES, the E-minis chart.

118
00:06:18,010 --> 00:06:19,390
You know, we hit a high here at 836.

119
00:06:19,390 --> 00:06:21,710
You know, we got up to around the 1886 levels.

120
00:06:21,710 --> 00:06:27,890
It came off, you know, four or five points, and we tried to make a run back up.

121
00:06:27,970 --> 00:06:31,150
You know, you got a green candle starting to run back up, but the price is being rejected here.

122
00:06:31,190 --> 00:06:34,630
You have a single print, you know, you have the ratio, and the market sells off.

123
00:06:34,630 --> 00:06:36,531
Okay, it sort of stops, and again,

124
00:06:36,531 --> 00:06:38,703
you know, people want to try and take

125
00:06:38,703 --> 00:06:40,604
it higher. But, again, it stopped here

126
00:06:40,604 --> 00:06:43,048
with this, at this level, with the single print.

127
00:06:43,170 --> 00:06:48,390
It's sort of circling around to this area where you have the, you know, the price rejection the first time.

128
00:06:48,450 --> 00:06:49,430
It does get a little bit through.

129
00:06:49,570 --> 00:06:51,357
So, you know, at this time, the second

130
00:06:51,357 --> 00:06:52,697
time, it is trying to get,

131
00:06:52,697 --> 00:06:54,708
you know, a little bit higher, and it does.

132
00:06:54,710 --> 00:07:00,070
But, you know, buyers are rejecting these levels above 1883.

133
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:04,310
You know, there's no more follow-through, and the market sells off.

134
00:07:08,310 --> 00:07:12,155
Now, a common way to trade price rejection is to trade it

135
00:07:12,155 --> 00:07:16,000
to a level of price acceptance, which basically translates to you get

136
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:22,409
into the trade around an area where there's price rejection, and you enter in an area where there's price acceptance.

137
00:07:22,410 --> 00:07:26,490
While there's nothing wrong with that approach, it does leave money on the table.

138
00:07:27,390 --> 00:07:36,650
I think, you know, sometimes it's hard to determine where price acceptance is. It's easier to determine price rejection.

139
00:07:38,190 --> 00:07:43,350
But, you know, order flows will allow you to trade from one price rejection to another.

140
00:07:44,510 --> 00:07:47,676
You know, so from an area, rather than going from

141
00:07:47,676 --> 00:07:50,842
an area where price is being rejected to an area

142
00:07:50,842 --> 00:07:53,374
where price is being accepted, it might be

143
00:07:53,374 --> 00:08:01,289
more prudent to go from an area where price is being rejected in one direction versus where price is being rejected in the opposite direction.

144
00:08:02,730 --> 00:08:06,294
You know, because as the market moves up or down, it'll go

145
00:08:06,294 --> 00:08:08,670
from a high at the top to the

146
00:08:08,670 --> 00:08:14,908
middle area where price is going to be accepted, and then go down to an area where price is being rejected.

147
00:08:14,910 --> 00:08:17,628
Wouldn't you rather trade from the high to the low

148
00:08:17,628 --> 00:08:19,803
rather from the high to the middle of

149
00:08:19,803 --> 00:08:24,968
the range than, you know, try and trade it from the middle of the range down to the low?

150
00:08:25,030 --> 00:08:26,790
It's just easier to trade from the high to the low.

151
00:08:27,510 --> 00:08:28,930
That's where you're going to make a lot of money.

152
00:08:30,330 --> 00:08:35,809
So remember, if price was accepted at a certain level, it would trade longer around there or move beyond that level.

153
00:08:35,809 --> 00:08:38,627
Now, by reading the order flow, you can see if the market

154
00:08:38,627 --> 00:08:40,975
is rejecting that price because there won't be a flow

155
00:08:40,975 --> 00:08:44,028
of orders coming into the market to move the market beyond that price.

156
00:08:45,910 --> 00:08:50,610
A perfect example here is a crude order chart, crude oil chart.

157
00:08:50,750 --> 00:08:51,510
You know, the market moved up.

158
00:08:51,570 --> 00:08:53,530
We hit a high, but price is rejected up there.

159
00:08:53,630 --> 00:08:56,470
You only got to, you know, where's the follow-through as you're going higher?

160
00:08:56,950 --> 00:08:59,254
You've got three lots traded right on the

161
00:08:59,254 --> 00:09:00,982
high, and, you know, buyers are

162
00:09:00,982 --> 00:09:04,150
rejecting these higher prices. You know, there's no more buying interest.

163
00:09:04,150 --> 00:09:05,690
The market starts to come off.

164
00:09:06,010 --> 00:09:08,430
Again, it tries to poke back higher.

165
00:09:08,550 --> 00:09:09,730
Again, it's rejecting price.

166
00:09:09,810 --> 00:09:14,110
You can see here in the single print of two lots, you know, there's no more follow-throughs.

167
00:09:14,170 --> 00:09:17,370
It's rejecting prices above $34.14, and the market sells off.

168
00:09:21,500 --> 00:09:25,100
Now, when the market is underpriced or overpriced, the institutional traders generally

169
00:09:25,100 --> 00:09:27,500
will come in and buy or sell to

170
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:31,400
bring back the market to a price level where more trade can occur.

171
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:34,220
So what are the signs of price rejection?

172
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:36,560
Well, there's basically two signs.

173
00:09:36,560 --> 00:09:38,400
And, you know, at first glance,

174
00:09:38,400 --> 00:09:40,240
you'll think that they're complete opposites,

175
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:42,080
but, you know, you have to

176
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:43,920
approach it in the same way.

177
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:48,720
It can be low volume at edges of a bar or heavy volume at edges of a bar.

178
00:09:51,070 --> 00:09:54,120
Low volume at edges of an up bar occur because

179
00:09:54,120 --> 00:09:58,390
there's no longer any more buyers to sustain the move. The market is overvalued.

180
00:09:59,650 --> 00:10:02,945
Low volume at the bottom of a down bar occurs

181
00:10:02,945 --> 00:10:06,569
when there's no longer any more interest from sellers in selling.

182
00:10:06,570 --> 00:10:09,190
So, I mean, think about that, okay?

183
00:10:09,250 --> 00:10:16,290
If a market is on the way up but there's no more buying interest, what's happening?

184
00:10:17,030 --> 00:10:19,470
You know, buyers are thinking the market is too rich.

185
00:10:19,470 --> 00:10:23,510
And conversely, if the market is going lower, what's going

186
00:10:23,510 --> 00:10:26,742
to cause the price to turn is going

187
00:10:26,742 --> 00:10:31,590
to be that, you know, there's no more sellers in the market.

188
00:10:31,590 --> 00:10:33,401
You know, yeah, technically that isn't

189
00:10:33,401 --> 00:10:35,212
necessarily price rejection, but if, you

190
00:10:35,212 --> 00:10:37,023
know, there's no more sellers in

191
00:10:37,023 --> 00:10:40,041
the market, you know, people that are selling the market

192
00:10:40,041 --> 00:10:43,059
are thinking, you know, there's no more capacity for them

193
00:10:43,059 --> 00:10:46,077
to make any money by selling there. So, if they

194
00:10:46,077 --> 00:10:54,528
stop selling, you know, they're rejecting those little prices and the market should, you know, bounce up to a level where they could be happy to sell again.

195
00:10:55,430 --> 00:10:57,250
So, you know, here's a five-year chart.

196
00:10:59,190 --> 00:11:02,450
And, you know, you've got a couple things going on in here.

197
00:11:04,110 --> 00:11:05,558
You have down here at 812

198
00:11:05,558 --> 00:11:07,296
and you've got a single print.

199
00:11:07,296 --> 00:11:12,799
You know, the market was working its way down and sellers were rejecting, you know, this area in here.

200
00:11:13,090 --> 00:11:14,850
They weren't interested in selling anymore.

201
00:11:15,570 --> 00:11:16,950
In this case, you know, buyers came in.

202
00:11:16,990 --> 00:11:19,863
You've got a few buying imbalances and the

203
00:11:19,863 --> 00:11:22,736
market trades up to, again, this level up

204
00:11:22,736 --> 00:11:26,328
here where buyers have now sort of changed their thoughts.

205
00:11:26,590 --> 00:11:34,730
You know, above 20.5, you know, they think it's probably too expensive and the market starts to come off.

206
00:11:34,830 --> 00:11:36,607
You know, maybe the buyers are stepping in

207
00:11:36,607 --> 00:11:40,829
again thinking, hey, let's make another run up at this high and see if we can take it higher.

208
00:11:41,130 --> 00:11:43,010
But, you know, they can't follow through.

209
00:11:43,950 --> 00:11:45,958
And, you know, what I was talking about

210
00:11:45,958 --> 00:11:48,468
earlier, rather than buying from an area down, you know,

211
00:11:48,468 --> 00:11:50,978
at the low to a level of price acceptance, you

212
00:11:50,978 --> 00:11:53,488
know, somewhere in here, you trade it from, you know,

213
00:11:53,488 --> 00:11:58,508
an area of price rejection to the next area of price rejection down to the next area of price rejection.

214
00:12:00,290 --> 00:12:02,978
You know, it's one of those things where

215
00:12:02,978 --> 00:12:05,330
rather than necessarily leave money on the

216
00:12:05,330 --> 00:12:12,050
table, you can trade it from rejection to rejection if, you know, if everything sort of sets up that way.

217
00:12:12,050 --> 00:12:15,308
So, heavy volume occurring at the edges of

218
00:12:15,308 --> 00:12:21,009
a bar are also a sign of rejection, even though that doesn't make sense.

219
00:12:21,110 --> 00:12:24,410
Most people feel that heavy volume would be a level of acceptance.

220
00:12:24,410 --> 00:12:26,700
But, when the market cannot get through, get

221
00:12:26,700 --> 00:12:28,990
past a level and turns, one side of

222
00:12:28,990 --> 00:12:34,429
the market has thrown in the towel and they gave up. They rejected the market. They rejected those prices.

223
00:12:34,430 --> 00:12:37,648
When heavy volume occurs at the bottom of a move

224
00:12:37,648 --> 00:12:40,223
down, sellers were met with strong passive buying

225
00:12:40,223 --> 00:12:44,729
and could not get the market to move past that level and gave up.

226
00:12:44,730 --> 00:12:47,752
You know, in the opposite way of thinking, when the

227
00:12:47,752 --> 00:12:50,774
heavy volume occurs at the top of an up move,

228
00:12:50,774 --> 00:12:58,028
buyers were met with strong passive selling and could not get the market to move up any further until all the buyers gave up.

229
00:12:58,030 --> 00:13:04,030
Now, what that looks like on an order flow chart is going to be often heavy volume.

230
00:13:04,490 --> 00:13:11,190
Now, people say that it's trapped traders, but, you know, you've got to realize what it is.

231
00:13:11,250 --> 00:13:14,092
The market is rallying and there's heavy volume

